  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Migration Data Portal &#x2013; Phase V</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Migration Data Portal is entering its fifth year. It is now an established and widely used source of migration data and analysis. While online portals and platforms proliferate, the Global Migration Data Analysis Centre (GMDAC) Portal remains unique: it collates and curates migration data from 25 leading international data providers worldwide. The earlier phases of the Portal helped to establish its foundational functions, features, and content, which have continued to grow and expand. Going forward, the next phase of the Portal is implementing a series of activities aimed towards: improved operational efficiency, including through adopting new technologies; new content on emerging and niche topics, while ensuring existing content is continuously updated in a timely manner; and raised awareness on the Portal and promoting interactive engagement with data users.Under these three pillars, activities outlined in this proposal include, inter alia: incorporating technologies to the Portal that facilitate data collection and sharing (Application Programming Interface (API), web-scraping, widgets); updating existing content and adding new content (English, French, German, Spanish) and adding datasets for further analysis, comparisons and visualizations; and implementing online trainings and webinars on migration data, conducting outreach campaigns and systematizing feedback.</narrative>
  </description>
